"""TenantWall flashcards: facts from tenantwall-explained.pdf and the 17 Nov 2026 real-AWS run (used by anki.py)."""
CARDS = [
 ("TenantWall: the problem in one line", "Several teams share one AWS account; without controls any user with EC2/S3 rights could touch another team's servers and files."),
 ("TenantWall: why ABAC instead of a role or policy per team?", "One policy set compares tags (Team on user = Team on resource), so adding a team means adding tags, not new identity policies."),
 ("TenantWall: the four layers", "Tagged IAM users; TenantABAC_EC2; TenantABAC_S3 (own prefix only); a bucket policy with explicit denies (other prefixes, non-TLS)."),
 ("What is ${aws:PrincipalTag/Team}?", "A policy variable replaced at request time by the caller's Team tag, so one policy works for every team."),
 ("Explicit deny vs implicit deny", "Explicit: a Deny statement matched and it beats every Allow. Implicit: no Allow matched (the default for everything)."),
 ("Order of IAM evaluation (same account)", "Start denied; any matching Deny → explicit deny; else any matching Allow (identity or resource policy) → allow; else implicit deny."),
 ("Why TenantWall uses explicit denies as well as missing allows", "Defence in depth: the Deny still blocks even if someone later adds a too-broad Allow."),
 ("TenantABAC_EC2: ReadOnlyEverywhere", "Allow ec2:Describe* on *; Describe calls do not support resource-level limits, so teams can see (not act on) all instances."),
 ("TenantABAC_EC2: ManageOnlyOwnTeamInstances", "Allow Start/Stop/Reboot/Terminate only where ec2:ResourceTag/Team equals ${aws:PrincipalTag/Team}."),
 ("TenantABAC_EC2: LaunchOnlyIfTaggedWithOwnTeamAndSmallType", "Allow RunInstances only if the request tags Team = your team (aws:RequestTag/Team) and the type is t2.micro or t3.micro."),
 ("TenantABAC_EC2: RunInstancesSupportingResources", "Allow RunInstances on every resource except the instance (NotResource): image, subnet, security group, volume, network interface."),
 ("TenantABAC_EC2: TagOnlyAtCreation", "Allow CreateTags only when ec2:CreateAction = RunInstances, so tags cannot be changed after launch."),
 ("TenantABAC_EC2: NoSelfPromotion", "Explicit Deny on iam:TagUser, UntagUser, PutUserPolicy, AttachUserPolicy, AddUserToGroup: a user cannot change their own Team tag or rights."),
 ("TenantABAC_EC2: DecodeOwnDenials", "Allow sts:DecodeAuthorizationMessage so a user can read why EC2 refused them."),
 ("TenantABAC_S3: what does it allow?", "Get/Put/DeleteObject under bucket/${aws:PrincipalTag/Team}/*, and ListBucket only when s3:prefix is the caller's own team prefix."),
 ("Bucket policy: DenyNonTLS", "Deny everything when aws:SecureTransport is false: no plain-HTTP access (scenario 13, explicit)."),
 ("Bucket policy: OnlyBetaTouchesBetaPrefix", "Deny any S3 action on beta/* unless the caller's Team tag is beta or the caller is the admin; alpha reading beta/secret.txt is an explicit deny."),
 ("Two conditions in one statement: AND or OR?", "AND. Several values for the same key inside one condition are OR."),
 ("How do you tell explicit from implicit for an EC2 refusal?", "Decode the encoded message with aws sts decode-authorization-message; it shows explicitDeny true or false."),
 ("Which TenantWall scenarios are explicit denies?", "9 (self-tag, NoSelfPromotion), 11 (read beta's file, bucket policy), 13 (plain HTTP, DenyNonTLS)."),
 ("Which TenantWall scenarios are implicit denies?", "2, 3, 4 (bad launches), 6 (stop beta's server), 8 (re-tag), 12 (list beta/), 14 (simulator terminate)."),
 ("Scenario 8: alpha re-tags its instance to Team=beta. Result and why?", "Refused, implicit: CreateTags is allowed only during RunInstances (TagOnlyAtCreation)."),
 ("Scenario 12: alpha lists beta/. Result and why?", "Refused, implicit: ListBucket is allowed only for the alpha/ prefix."),
 ("What does DryRun do in EC2?", "Checks permissions without acting: DryRunOperation = would be allowed; UnauthorizedOperation = refused."),
 ("CloudTrail management events vs data events", "Management: control-plane calls (RunInstances, TagUser, PutBucketPolicy). Data: object-level calls like S3 GetObject/PutObject; off by default and billed."),
 ("Why TenantWall enables S3 data events", "Without them, reads of another team's files (GetObject) would not be recorded."),
 ("CloudTrail log file validation", "Signed digest files prove the log files were not changed or deleted."),
 ("CloudWatch metric filter: AccessDenied pattern", "{ ($.errorCode = \"AccessDenied*\") || ($.errorCode = \"*UnauthorizedOperation\") }: $. reads a JSON field, * wildcard, || OR."),
 ("TenantWall alarm settings", "Sum over 300 s, 1 evaluation period, threshold ≥ 1, missing data = not breaching; action: publish to the SNS topic."),
 ("Alarm states", "OK (below threshold), ALARM (breached), INSUFFICIENT_DATA (not enough data yet)."),
 ("What does SNS do in TenantWall?", "The alarm publishes to the topic; SNS emails every confirmed subscriber."),
 ("What did IAM Access Analyzer report for TenantWall's policies?", "No errors, security warnings, warnings or suggestions for TenantABAC_EC2, TenantABAC_S3 and the bucket policy."),
 ("TenantWall real run (17 Nov 2026): results", "14 of 14 scenarios as expected; AccessDenied and TagTampering alarms fired with email; PolicyChange stayed OK."),
 ("TenantWall: how fast were refusals reported?", "Events reached CloudWatch Logs in 63–130 s (S3 data events about 316 s); AccessDenied alarm 143 s after the first refusal, TagTampering 104 s after TagUser."),
 ("TenantWall: a false alert you saw", "About 30 min later two refused console calls with no tenant user raised AccessDenied again; fix: scope the filter to tenant principals."),
 ("TenantWall limitations", "Shared Describe visibility, trust in correct tagging, minutes of CloudTrail delay, bucket policy grows per team (size limit), one small evaluation."),
]
